  "articleBody": "When you're trying to spruce up your home with interior paint and drywall fixes, it's easy to make a few common missteps that can sabotage your efforts. Here are some mistakes to steer clear of: First, never patch over active leaks or mildew. This is a big no-no! If there's moisture, you must find and fix the source first, otherwise your repair won't last, and you could be creating bigger problems like mold. Second, don't fail to confirm the source of staining or drywall failure. Just painting over a stain without knowing why it's there is like putting a band-aid on a gushing wound. Always investigate. Third, leaving the repair incomplete by skipping steps like primer, proper sanding, or touch-up paint. These aren't optional; they're crucial for a smooth, durable, and seamless finish. A patchy repair sticks out like a sore thumb. Fourth, trying to match finishes (like paint or drywall texture) without enough care. It takes a keen eye and sometimes specialized tools to blend everything perfectly. If the damage is widespread, tied to moisture, or involves complex drywall or ceiling issues, that's when a professional really comes in handy. HH Remodeling LLC in the Denver area can help ensure your interior repairs are done right. Don't hesitate to reach out to us at 303-505-0866.",
